# CR 712.9, 701.27c: only a permanent represented by a double-faced card can transform. Bot2's Clone enters as a copy of
# Bot1's Delver of Secrets and has its upkeep ability; at Bot2's turn-4 upkeep it reveals Lightning Bolt, an instant, and
# "transform this creature" does nothing: Clone is not a double-faced card, so it stays a 1/1 Delver of Secrets (the
# rule's Wildblood Pack example). Bot1 keeps its own top card hidden on turn 3.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Delver of Secrets
Island x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Clone
Island x4
Island
Lightning Bolt
Island x11

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Delver of Secrets.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Clone.Cast
Bot2.Accept
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]
Bot1.Decline
[T4 Bot2.Upkeep]
? Stack = Delver of Secrets
Bot2.Accept
? Bot2.Revealed = Lightning Bolt
[T4 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Delver of Secrets
Bot2.Battlefield.Delver of Secrets.Power = 1
Bot2.Battlefield.Delver of Secrets.Keywords = (absent)
Bot2.Revealed = Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Delver of Secrets
